{
  "slug": "mbos",
  "title": "MERCEDES - MBOS",
  "description": "Translating Mercedes-Benz luxury into the digital space with MB.OS: visual metaphors in metal and glass instead of feature lists.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "d5a816f7",
      "type": "hero",
      "media": {
        "kind": "video",
        "project": "mercedes02",
        "type": "header",
        "alt": "Animation of reflective metal and glass surfaces for Mercedes-Benz MB.OS"
      },
      "title": "Mercedes asked how to translate luxury into the digital space?",
      "intro": [
        "My answer was a simple visual framework. Instead of showcasing features we would create visual metaphors that encapsulate the sensorial experience of using them.",
        "Aesthetically I tied the two worlds together by reducing the visual palette of our artists to metal and glass. Metal carried the physicality the brand is known for — weight, precision, the tactile world of the cars themselves while glass stood in for the digital space — transparent, layered, a little more abstract. Together they form a synthesis of Mercedes new approach to Software.",
        "The result was a visual poem that underlined the brands commitment to . It was a toolkit that represented the brand in a new light."
      ],
      "credit": "Commissioned Work | Mercedes Benz | 2024 | **Creative Direction & Artist**"
    },
